      "topic": "Modulus of a complex number",
      "source": "TN HSE Mar 2024",
      "type": "mcq",
      "marks": 1,
      "q": "If $|z_1|=1$, $|z_2|=2$, $|z_3|=3$ and $|9z_1z_2+4z_1z_3+z_2z_3|=12$, then the value of $|z_1+z_2+z_3|$ is :",
      "options": [
        "3",
        "1",
        "4",
        "2"
      ],
      "answer": 3,
      "solution": "Since $|z_k|^2=z_k\\bar z_k$: $9z_1z_2+4z_1z_3+z_2z_3=z_1z_2z_3\\left(\\dfrac{9}{z_3}+\\dfrac{4}{z_2}+\\dfrac{1}{z_1}\\right)=z_1z_2z_3(\\bar z_3+\\bar z_2+\\bar z_1)$.\n\nTaking moduli: $12=1\\cdot2\\cdot3\\cdot|z_1+z_2+z_3|$, so $|z_1+z_2+z_3|=2$."
    },
    {
